# deadpool_pro 1.16 - drafted by port_tool.py from jaws_le-1.02.port, finished with call_probe.c and the
# end-of-ball hook (item 138). Lights, screens and clips are off: their functions were not found.
# Emulator-proven 2026-09-24 by a full build check (modes/gamecheck.sh play full, item 162): the
# runtime hooked the game, 25 of its 25 shots came from their switches, a drain ended each ball, and
# the 8 events below fired where their names say (a tilted ball, three balls to the game's end).
# Callouts heard in the emulator 2026-09-25 (item 164, the item 163 pipeline): countdown.

game           deadpool_pro
version        1.16

# ---- functions: site <name> <address> <first two instruction words> --------------------
site tick             0x0021c3ec 0xe92d4038 0xe3a00037
#   shot_dispatch: cmode_manager virtual 11 (0xff9c4), found with call_probe.c: once per press, the mask
#   64-bit in r2:r3 as on Godzilla (it walks 26 modes calling their +0x6c)
site shot_dispatch    0x000ff9c4 0xe92d4ff0 0xe1a07003
#   ball_end: 0xfe798, which the handler of hook 0x34 calls (registered 0x101180); it walks the 26 modes
#   calling their +0x40. Godzilla's handlers of hooks 0x34 and 0xc6 both call its ball_end
